Retro rules: iResolution is the fixed internal resolution, fragCoord in those pixels. Use 2D effects from `retro/effects.glsl` (plasma2, starfield, copperBar), `retro/font.glsl` for text scrollers (drawText with uText), work in display colors (palette hex / 255, never converted to linear) and finish with `fragColor = vec4(finalize(col, uv), 1.0);`: the style's finalize quantizes to its PALETTE, do not call retroFinalize with a palette of your own. Budget: p95 <= {{ budget_p95 }} ms at {{ res }}.
Light 3D only if perf_tier=light. No heavy raymarching. Cost limit: at most {{ max_ref_ratio }}x a reference raymarched tunnel at the same resolution.

Anti-cliché (retro): no generic full-screen rainbow plasma, no plain sine scroller, copper bar only as one element, no rainbow palette without art direction.
Avoid: {{ spec.avoid | join(", ") }}
Scroller text (if any): {{ spec.text }}

Follow the contract prefix EXACTLY (envelope with one ```json + one ```glsl block; only mainImage body).

## Math oracle (optional, encouraged)
Same as modern: emit verified formulas in `math_requests` (kind sdf|lipschitz|periodic_path|easing|identity, python-safe `expr` over `inputs`, `claim` with domain/tol). Accepted requests become callable GLSL functions named by `id`.
